As I said, the title is a ruse to get you to buy the book and learn something 
about Dyribal and other interesting languages.  Labov was doing the same thing
with the talk I mentioned.  I would guess that Lakoff has
had his heart broken enough times by a woman (and once is enough!) to know 
how effective the title would be on a hetero male audience.  I sometimes
wonder whether my female guests would be offended (or intrigued) by seeing the
book on my bookshelf.  If Nan's reaction is any indication, I should probably
hide it along with my back-issues of _Playboy_.

BTW, Dyribal puts men in the same category with snakes.  And boomerangs.

