Subject: [#94-3-160] Philo: My Transformation (no hair)

I am writing about a transformation I undertook one week ago.

I am writing about it because I think it puts an interesting light on
several extropian topics. For example, if one is uploaded into a
computer, or if a copy of a person is made, we have often asked, "How
does the copy/upload know who they are." Another question, might be,
"If I am frozen and then brought back, how do I know I am "me." "

I can't answer those questions, but I can talk about what I did
that was far less traumatic (and probably a lot less interesting).

I had almost 100% of the hair on my body removed by a waxing. I had a
lot of body hair, and in fact it took about 3 1/2 hours for the waxing
to take place. When I was done, i still had hair on my head, my arm
pits, and my "balls." That's it.

It was a painful experience, but not that painful. Still it was
traumatic; having to get naked in front of a stranger, having one's
hair pulled for 3 1/2 hours, etc.

The strange part was when I was done.

1) I didn't feel like me.

2) I didn't (when looking at my naked body) look like me.

3) When I walked around the way my skin (sans-hair) interacted
   with my clothes didn't feel like me.

4) Also hair seems to help my body deal with shifting and changing
   temperatures and moisture levels - without the hair I felt very
   strange almost "clammy."

5) When I type at the keyboard and see my hands in front of me,
   they don't look like my hands (all smooth with no hair). This
   I notice almost everyday.

As far as I know I wasn't upload during the waxing. As far as I know
I am still me. As far as I believe, if I was upload I would still be
me, but I wonder if I would feel like me.

/hawk


